      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8709257::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 300°C represents the proposed normal PWR-water test condition.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Steam exposure at approximately 1100–1200°C represents the proposed accident-relevant test condition.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8709257::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al addition will cause in situ formation of a dense, stable Al2O3 layer at or near the Cr–Zr interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al incorporated into Cr preferentially oxidizes because of its strong affinity for oxygen.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preferential oxidation of Al will form a continuous alumina barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina barrier will reduce Cr–Zr interdiffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced Cr–Zr interdiffusion will retard coating delamination or premature failure during high-temperature steam oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to pure Cr, the Cr–Al coating will show reduced interfacial element transport.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to pure Cr, the Cr–Al coating will show enhanced oxidation resistance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8709257::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to pure Cr, the Cr–Al coating will show better adhesion and coating integrity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elemental Cr coatings can peel and crack during high-temperature steam oxidation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elemental Cr coatings provide good corrosion protection in normal subcritical water or high-temperature steam.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will remain effective around 300°C and during short-to-moderate steam exposures at 1100–1200°C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
